# Keep the build context to what Dockerfile.dash actually COPYs. Without this, `out/` alone
# (step frames, recordings, 1.4 GB on a working laptop) is uploaded to the builder on every
# build — the exact bulk the snapshot exists to leave behind.
.git
node_modules
dist-electron
out
tests
docs
native/axdom
native/liveview
native/default-browser
tools
*.png
*.mp4
.env
.DS_Store
# The fleet's addresses and pinned host keys have no business in an image that cannot use them.
hosts.json
# Snapshots other than the one being shipped (SNAPSHOT_DIR selects it; the rest are noise).
snapshots/*
!snapshots/current
# The snapshot's cursor renders MUST reach the builder — the dash's /api/video serves them, and
# a row offering a take that 404s is worse than one that never offered it.
#
# Stated explicitly rather than relied upon: `*.mp4` above should not match a nested path (these
# patterns match whole relative paths, and `*` does not cross a separator), so this ought to be a
# no-op — but "ought to" is the wrong footing for a rule whose failure mode is silent. Last match
# wins, so this settles it either way.
!snapshots/current/**/*.mp4
